Hisense A6L audio-20261010 (10 Oct 2026, firmware/extracted/audio-20261010) for the AOSP AIDL example audio HAL
(ModulePrimary): accept the connection of the analog 3.5 mm jack devices (Wired Headset / Wired Headphones / Wired Headset
Mic). Without it IModule.connectExternalDevice failed in Module::populateConnectedDevicePort (EX_ILLEGAL_STATE), the audio
policy dropped the device and media and calls stayed on the speaker. Apply after 0002 (same files), in hardware/interfaces,
by tools/rom-v2-pipeline.sh (audio/patches/*.patch).

diff -ru a/audio/aidl/default/ModulePrimary.cpp b/audio/aidl/default/ModulePrimary.cpp
--- a/audio/aidl/default/ModulePrimary.cpp	2026-10-10 10:14:21.009370145 +0200
+++ b/audio/aidl/default/ModulePrimary.cpp	2026-10-10 10:14:21.012778534 +0200
@@ -237,6 +237,28 @@
     return Module::setMicMute(in_mute);
 }
 
+// Hisense A6L audio-20261010 (firmware/extracted/audio-20261010): the 3.5 mm jack. audio_policy_configuration.xml declares
+// "Wired Headset", "Wired Headphones" and "Wired Headset Mic" as external (non-attached) device ports of this module, so
+// the audio policy connects them with IModule.connectExternalDevice when WiredAccessoryManager reports the jack. The
+// default Module::populateConnectedDevicePort() refuses every device with a connection type (EX_ILLEGAL_STATE, "module
+// implementation must override 'populateConnectedDevicePort'"), so the connection failed, the policy dropped the device
+// and media/calls stayed on the speaker/earpiece (and no BECOMING_NOISY on unplug: the headset never was the music
+// device). Analog jack devices need nothing from the HAL: the ports keep their static profiles (the PCM is the same
+// MultiMedia1 front end) and the codec path is switched by a6l-audio-route from vendor.a6l.audio.media_out/call_out.
+ndk::ScopedAStatus ModulePrimary::populateConnectedDevicePort(AudioPort* audioPort, int32_t nextPortId) {
+    if (audioPort->ext.getTag() == AudioPortExt::device) {
+        const auto& type = audioPort->ext.get<AudioPortExt::device>().device.type;
+        if (type.connection == AudioDeviceDescription::CONNECTION_ANALOG &&
+            (type.type == AudioDeviceType::OUT_HEADSET || type.type == AudioDeviceType::OUT_HEADPHONE ||
+             type.type == AudioDeviceType::IN_HEADSET)) {
+            LOG(INFO) << __func__ << ": A6L wired jack device " << type.toString() << " connected (port id "
+                      << nextPortId << ", static profiles)";
+            return ndk::ScopedAStatus::ok();
+        }
+    }
+    return Module::populateConnectedDevicePort(audioPort, nextPortId);
+}
